# Pairs with DivergenceAccounted in SchemaCrossRegion. Strict ingest diverts a refused entry
# without writing its dead-letter record, so the receiver lacks the row for good and nothing
# accounts for the divergence (the record is what the operator inspects and re-submits).
MODULE: DivergenceAccountedDivertWithoutRecord
TARGET: DivergenceAccounted
CLASS: Invariant
SUMMARY: a diverted entry leaves no dead-letter record, so its divergence is unaccounted
PERTURBS: Deliver

--- FIND
    /\ dl' = [dl EXCEPT ![e] = IF st'[e] = "Diverted" THEN 1 ELSE @]
--- REPLACE
\* MUTATION: the diversion writes no dead letter.
    /\ UNCHANGED dl
--- END